; d3d11_x.def — ERA (Xbox One) D3D11.x import lib (phase 5).
; The layer translates these to a real desktop D3D11 device; see
; docs/ERA-GDK-MAPPING.md. D3D11XCreateDeviceX's 3-arg form
; (params struct, device, context) is GROUNDED in WinDurango's public
; d3d11.x.cpp (XDK-derived). D3DMapEsramMemory and DXGIXPresentArray
; signatures are grounded in the same source.
; Ordinals are WinDurango's d3d11_x.dll ordinals (dumpbin /exports
; 2026-11-23): D3D11XCreateDeviceX @4, D3DMapEsramMemory @9,
; DXGIXPresentArray @11. The FH2 exe's import table gives HINTS
; (3, 8, 10) — a hint is an index into the sorted export-name table,
; NOT an ordinal. The real console ordinals are unknown; WinDurango's
; layout is the only available one. The exe imports by NAME, so the
; ordinal rows never affect it — they only matter for a title that
; imports by ordinal.
; D3D11XCreateDevice / D3D11XCreateDeviceAndSwapChain have no known
; real ordinal (the real FH2 exe does not import them) and export by
; name only. D3DAllocateGraphicsMemory / D3DFreeGraphicsMemory are
; supporting infrastructure (WinDurango ordinals 6 / 8, but the exe
; does not import them) and also export by name only.
LIBRARY d3d11_x
EXPORTS
    D3D11XCreateDevice
    D3D11XCreateDeviceAndSwapChain
    D3D11XCreateDeviceX @4
    D3DMapEsramMemory @9
    DXGIXPresentArray @11
    D3DAllocateGraphicsMemory
    D3DFreeGraphicsMemory
